WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.836 --> 00:00:03.762
The filling unit of line 3 sometimes fails.

2
00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:06.347
Then the whole line stands still.

3
00:00:07.352 --> 00:00:10.255
The module Reliability and asset strategy is

4
00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:13.122
about how parts fail and what you do about it.

5
00:00:14.177 --> 00:00:15.408
You are the engineer.

6
00:00:16.104 --> 00:00:19.761
After the shift you and the team lead make the unit more reliable.

7
00:00:20.748 --> 00:00:24.359
First you know how parts fail and which part weighs most.

8
00:00:25.471 --> 00:00:29.105
Then you choose which maintenance fits and let the numbers decide.

9
00:00:30.402 --> 00:00:33.037
The first topic is Failure and its patterns.

10
00:00:33.748 --> 00:00:36.697
First you look at how a part of the unit fails.

11
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.213
A handy picture is that a part fails when

12
00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:42.628
the load on it is higher than its strength.

13
00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:45.150
Wear usually gives a warning.

14
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.577
A sudden overload does not.

15
00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:52.323
You read the pattern in the failure data from the shape parameter.

16
00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:56.851
The second topic is F M E A and criticality.

17
00:00:57.562 --> 00:00:59.420
Not every part counts the same.

18
00:01:00.436 --> 00:01:04.151
You look at what happens when it fails, and how likely that is.

19
00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:09.390
You put the parts in a risk matrix and make an FMECA.

20
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.261
The marked cell stands for a big consequence and a high likelihood.

21
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.601
You tackle that part first.

22
00:01:17.928 --> 00:01:21.028
The third topic is RCM and asset strategy.

23
00:01:21.718 --> 00:01:24.888
You choose which maintenance each part really needs.

24
00:01:25.905 --> 00:01:29.261
You start with what the unit must do, with a standard in it.

25
00:01:30.293 --> 00:01:33.149
A protection can fail without anyone noticing.

26
00:01:34.186 --> 00:01:36.821
For that you schedule a failure-finding task.

27
00:01:38.155 --> 00:01:41.417
The fourth topic is Reliability data and decisions.

28
00:01:42.124 --> 00:01:44.318
You let the numbers say what pays off.

29
00:01:45.322 --> 00:01:49.443
You count how often the unit fails and how long it then stands still.

30
00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:54.585
In many plants waiting is the biggest share of the downtime, not the repair.

31
00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.385
You work out the operational availability.

32
00:01:59.373 --> 00:02:02.810
That is how you make the unit more reliable, where it counts.

33
00:02:04.132 --> 00:02:04.991
The whole map.

34
00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:10.937
The fourth station is Reliability and asset strategy, in Making the plant better.

35
00:02:11.963 --> 00:02:13.705
Each topic has four levels.

36
00:02:14.713 --> 00:02:17.859
Start at Basics level with how parts physically fail.

37
00:02:18.582 --> 00:02:20.405
It shows what breaks and why.

38
00:02:21.436 --> 00:02:26.034
At Working knowledge level come reading failure data, F M E A on plant,

39
00:02:26.173 --> 00:02:28.472
RCM and where the downtime goes.

40
00:02:29.495 --> 00:02:31.747
At Advanced level come root causes,

41
00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.648
standby units, a reliability programme and spare parts.

42
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.384
At Expert level come fitting life data, risk in euros,

43
00:02:40.605 --> 00:02:42.997
asset management and life-cycle cost.
